; Demanded producer is a mutable(...) KV merge (RegionalDataFlowCore test
; matrix C5). The bound #query bal_of reads balance, whose value column is
; mutable(add_u32) -- a KV index (the degenerate aggregate). Under -demand
; (this case's .drflags) the demand transform tries to materialize the
; demanded producer, but a KV/aggregate view is a single derived relation the
; flat guard web cannot re-root, so the pass rejects with the R-MAT "single
; derived relation" diagnostic in all 4 optimization modes. This is NOT the
; V-ALGEBRA reject: add_u32 DECLARES its algebra (@invertible), so the KV
; merge is well-formed -- the reject is purely the demand-over-KV fence.
;
; The oracle referees the DEFINITIONAL answer of the PLAIN program (no
; -demand): the least model of the KV sum. credit is monotone (add-only), so
; value-churn here is accumulation -- several credits fold into one per-account
; balance via the @invertible add.
#functor add_u32(bound u32 L, bound u32 R, free u32 Res) @invertible.
#message credit(u64 Acct, u32 Amt).
#local entry(u64 Acct, u32 Amt).
entry(A, M) : credit(A, M).
#local balance(u64 Acct, mutable(add_u32) Amt).
balance(A, M) : entry(A, M).
#query bal_of(bound u64 Acct, free u32 Amt) : balance(Acct, Amt).
